  "answer": "Not especially. The Aussie is stronger against the yen than it was a year ago, though it has slipped from its recent highs.\n\n- **Latest:** A$1 bought ¥109.67 on 16 October 2026.\n- **Past year:** It was ¥100.84 at the end of October 2025, so the Aussie is up about 8.8% against the yen.\n- **Recent peak:** It reached about ¥114.3 in April and ¥114.5 in August. On 1 September it was ¥114.63, the high for that month.\n- **Recent drift:** It has fallen about 4.3% from that early-September level. It has been steady at ¥109–111 since mid-September.\n\nThe trade-weighted index shows a similar pattern. It was 64.4 in October, against 61.2 a year earlier and a recent high of 66.6 in May. So the Aussie is up on a year ago and a bit below its mid-2026 levels.\n\nThe data goes up to 16 October. It's a snapshot rather than a forecast.",
